{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For they rebelled against His spirit</b> — it returns to HaShem, as in \"and they rebelled and grieved His holy spirit.\"" "<b>And the meaning of \"and he spoke rashly\"</b> — concerning HaShem, who decreed upon Moses that he not enter the land; and it was an inadvertence on Moses' part because of his anger, as I explained in its place. And it is possible that \"his spirit\" is the spirit of Moses, and \"he spoke rashly\" — that he said to Israel, \"rebels,\" and forgot to speak, and struck; and it would have been fitting that the word not go forth from his mouth, until he completed the commandment of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:49.030600299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}